        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "YbCl3 (0.335 g, 1.20 mmol), ZnCl2 (0.164 g, 1.20 mmol) and L-leucine (0.159 g, 1.20 mmol) were mixed in aqueous solution. The pH was adjusted to ~6.0 by slow addition of several millilitres of 0.1 M NaOH with heating and stirring. The precipitate formed by partial hydrolysis of YbCl3 was filtered off and the filtrate was concentrated by slow evaporation at room temperature, giving colorless prismatic crystals after several weeks (yield 60% based on L-leucine).",
